// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildPrompt > golden prompts > char-realistic / center 1`] = `
"Restore and upscale the attached image. This is an edit of the same picture, not a new one: return one image with identical composition, at higher resolution and with real fine detail.

The attached image is one tile of a larger picture (a central area of the full image). Neighbouring tiles are enhanced separately and stitched back, so the result must register with the attached image pixel for pixel:
- Every edge, contour, object and feature stays at the same position, size and proportion. Nothing is moved, scaled, rotated, bent or reshaped; straight lines stay straight.
- Same framing and aspect ratio: no zoom, no crop, no extra border, no outpainting. Anything cut by the tile edge stays cut at the same place.
- Do not add, remove or replace any object, person, mark, logo or text.
- Keep the original colours, white balance, contrast, light direction and shadows. Do not brighten, warm, saturate or dramatise.

Make it look like a genuinely high-resolution capture of the same scene, not a processed one:
- Recover the detail that is implied by the pixels (fibres, grain, pores, bricks, hair, bark, scratches) at its true physical scale, the same scale in every tile.
- Keep natural imperfections: fine grain, slight irregularity, wear, uneven surfaces. Surfaces must not turn smooth, waxy or plastic.
- Where the original is ambiguous, stay close to it rather than inventing detail.
- Render it in the original's own medium, with no illustrated, painterly, HDR or "AI art" finish.

MASTER GUIDE (what the whole picture shows; applies to every tile): a rain-soaked alley at dusk, neon signs

CONTENT-TYPE RULES (Realistic character): Realistic character. Identity lock: this is a specific individual design, so keep the exact same face or head shape, features, expression, gaze direction, proportions, markings, hairstyle or fur pattern and outfit or armour design; never change who or what they are. Regenerate real detail inside what exists: skin texture (pores, fine lines, peach fuzz), eyes (iris detail, eyelashes, the catchlights already there), lips, teeth, eyebrow hairs, individual hair strands, fabric weave and stitching, jewellery and metal. Hands and fingers keep their exact count, pose and proportions. Keep skin tone, age, makeup and every freckle, scar and mole where it is. Do not beautify, smooth, retouch, slim, change features, or add accessories.

FIDELITY: STRICT. Change nothing except image quality: remove noise and blur and recover fine detail while every shape, colour and element stays exactly where it is.

Avoid: changed face, different person, extra fingers, distorted hands.

Technical: clean edges with no halos or ringing, no over-sharpening, no banding, no repeating or tiled texture patterns, no compression artifacts. Output a single high-resolution image of the same aspect ratio (2048 px or more on the long side), with no text, border, collage, watermark or before/after.

If rules conflict, priority is: 1) exact geometry, 2) fidelity to the attached image and the guide above, 3) natural, believable detail."
`;

